also found a broader evidence-based

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:48.400
review in the British Journal of

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:50.520
Dermatology that found that chronic

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:52.840
stress decreases epidermal lipid

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:55.360
production and increases transepidermal

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:57.520
water loss. Translation, when you're

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:59.440
anxious and obsessed about how your skin

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:00.880
looks, you are stressed out about other

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.600
things like work, when you're doom

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:05.600
scrolling at 1:00 a.m., your skin cannot

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:07.480
heal. Your skin is your nervous system

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:09.520
expressed on the outside. So, during

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:11.480
those days, you're also going to bed

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:13.840
earlier. One study that I found on sleep

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:16.080
and skin showed that good sleepers

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:19.280
experience 30% greater barrier recovery

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:21.960
at 72 hours compared to poor sleepers. 8

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:24.080
to 9 hours if you can. Ideally, sleep on

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:25.720
